e-for-Edit-Distance-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L13"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nThere is one uniform randomized algorithm that, given $x,y$ and a rational\n$\\varepsilon\\in(0,1)$, returns a nonnegative integer $\\widehat D$ such that\n\\[\n \\Pr\\bigl[\\ED(x,y)\\le \\widehat D\\le(1+\\varepsilon)\\ED(x,y)\\bigr]\n \\ge \\frac23.\n\\]\nFor every fixed rational $\\varepsilon$, its worst-case expected running time\non strings of total length $N$ is $N^{1+o(1)}$ as $N\\to\\infty$ on the\nlogarithmic-word RAM. The expectation is over internal randomness only,\nand the bound includes input processing, preprocessing, numerical work,\nrandom sampling and all data-structure operations. Equal strings return zero\ndeterministically."},{"appendix":false,"contribution_target":{"fingerprint":"sha256:d2fdf192c1bc59997cafdc7b0fa51cb09f9569877a5c6aa9e99da0bc98b72273","grain":"paper-statement","id":"An-Almost-Linear-Approximation-Scheme-for-Edit-Distance-September-24-2026#thm:seed","title":"Initial estimates"},"credit":{"kind":"producer-declared","license":null,"license_status":"consult-source-notice","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","source":"lean/formalization.yaml","source_registry":"index.json#/sources"},"detail":{"path":"../rows/55eb8cc97fae91e4024275ba.json","pointer":"/row"},"display":"Theorem","id":"r:An-Almost-Linear-Approximation-Scheme-for-Edit-Distance-September-24-2026:thm:seed","manuscript_id":"p:An-Almost-Linear-Approximation-Scheme-for-Edit-Distance-September-24-2026","name":"Initial estimates","printed_number":"3.1","printed_number_provenance":{"atlas_pin":"755c4b729512c7e2c7d1d3303eb9706f5adf1681","binding":{"file":"build/sections/03-seed.tex","label":"thm:seed","line":10,"manuscript":"An-Almost-Linear-Approximation-Scheme-for-Edit-Distance-September-24-2026","statement_sha256":"214fea8ff8bf8fc0e96d60d832ebfbd1b52ef521b18c76980ca8ff2d3445dea1"},"blob_s